---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
import { getApps, appUrl } from '../lib/content';
const apps = await getApps();
const updated = new Date(site.privacyUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-AU', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
// BOILERPLATE: a sensible starting point for a small Australian software business.
// It is not legal advice: review it against what your apps really do.
---
<Base title="Privacy policy" description={`How ${site.legalName} collects, uses and protects personal information.`}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p>
        This policy explains how {site.legalName} ("Datavis", "we", "us") handles personal information when you
        use this website, our apps and our software. We aim to collect as little as possible. We handle personal
        information in line with the Australian Privacy Principles in the <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth).
      </p>

      {apps.length > 0 && (
        <p>
          Each app also has its own privacy page that lists exactly what that app collects:
          {apps.map((a, i) => <>{i > 0 && ', '}<a href={`${appUrl(a.id)}privacy/`}>{a.data.name}</a></>)}.
          Where an app's page says something more specific, it applies to that app.
        </p>
      )}

      <h2 id="collect">What we collect</h2>
      <h3>When you visit this website</h3>
      <p>
        This website does not use cookies, analytics, advertising or tracking scripts, and has no forms or
        accounts. Like every web server, our hosting provider may record standard technical logs (IP address,
        browser type, pages requested and time) to keep the service secure and running. We do not use these logs
        to identify you.
      </p>
      <h3>When you contact us</h3>
      <p>
        If you email us, we receive your email address, your name if you include it, and whatever you choose to
        tell us. We use it only to reply and to provide the support or service you asked for.
      </p>
      <h3>When you use our apps</h3>
      <p>
        Unless an app's privacy page says otherwise, our apps do not collect personal information, do not require
        an account, and keep your data on your device. Where an app does collect data, its privacy page lists the
        categories, why they are collected, and whether they are shared.
      </p>
      <h3>When you buy a commercial licence</h3>
      <p>
        We keep the name, business details, email address and licence details needed to issue and support your
        licence, and the records we are required to keep for tax purposes. Payments are processed by our payment
        provider; we do not see or store your full card details.
      </p>

      <h2 id="use">How we use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>to reply to you and provide support;</li>
        <li>to issue, manage and support licences;</li>
        <li>to keep our services secure and fix problems;</li>
        <li>to meet legal and tax obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell personal information, and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

      <h2 id="share">Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We share personal information only with service providers that help us run the business (for example
        email, hosting and payment providers), only as much as they need, or where the law requires it. Some
        of these providers may store data outside Australia, including in the United States. We choose providers
        that protect information to a standard similar to the Australian Privacy Principles.
      </p>

      <h2 id="security">How we protect it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep personal information in accounts protected by strong passwords and two-factor authentication,
        limit who can access it, and delete it when we no longer need it. No system is perfectly secure; if a
        data breach is likely to cause you serious harm, we will tell you and, where required, the Office of
        the Australian Information Commissioner.
      </p>

      <h2 id="retention">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep support emails for as long as needed to help you and for a reasonable time afterwards, and
        licence and financial records for as long as the law requires (generally five to seven years).
      </p>

      <h2 id="rights">Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see the personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete
        it, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.email.privacy}`}>{site.email.privacy}</a>. We will respond within
        30 days. If you are in the European Union, United Kingdom or a US state with privacy laws, you have
        similar rights under those laws, and we will honour them.
      </p>

      <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
      <p>
        Our apps and services are not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
        information from them. If you think a child has given us personal information, contact us and we will
        delete it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top of this page. If a change matters, for
        example an app starts collecting new data, we will say so in the app's release notes too.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact and complaints</h2>
      <p>
        {site.legalName}{site.abn && <> (ABN {site.abn})</>}, {site.country}. Email:
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email.privacy}`}>{site.email.privacy}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with our response to a privacy complaint, you can contact the
        <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="noopener">Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
